      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The park opened in 1912 as a memorial to Logan of the Seneca and Cayuga Tribes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://pickawaycountyparks.org/logan-elm-memorial-park/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A plaque marks the exact spot where Chief Logan delivered his lament about Indian and white‑man relations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
